WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.325
The variation printed in the rose is for the year it was measured.

2
00:00:04.575 --> 00:00:07.975
Sometimes the exam asks you to bring it up to date.

3
00:00:08.225 --> 00:00:10.100
Follow it on screen.

4
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:17.175
The rose says fourteen degrees, forty-five minutes west, in twenty ten, increasing two minutes a year.

5
00:00:17.425 --> 00:00:19.675
It’s now twenty twenty-six.

6
00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:22.200
So sixteen years have passed.

7
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.500
Sixteen times two minutes is thirty-two minutes of increase.

8
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.825
Fourteen degrees forty-five minutes, plus thirty-two minutes.

9
00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:33.250
Careful: carry at sixty.

10
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.425
Fifteen degrees, seventeen minutes west.

11
00:00:37.675 --> 00:00:40.750
For plotting, call it fifteen degrees west.

12
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.650
One warning.

13
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:47.200
Many exam questions simply hand you the variation to use.

14
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:51.875
If the question gives you a number, use that number, and skip this step.
